---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Projects | Grime Art, Wearables, XRPL Lore and Archive Lanes"
  description="Project lanes for NO BALL GAMES: Grime Art painted works, wearable art, collaboration direction, XRP KIDs lore branch and research archive development."
  current="projects"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Projects</span>
    <h1>Five core lanes, one street-rooted system.</h1>
    <p>
      The project map is built from the truth files: art first, wearables next, collab direction, XRP KIDs lore branch and the archive/research layer that keeps public claims disciplined.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section project-grid">
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lane 01</span>
      <h3>Grime Art / painted works</h3>
      <p>Original canvases, portrait studies, sign-flip pieces and graffiti-coded artworks shaped by Charlie Buster's raw UK visual language.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>View art collector lane →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lane 02</span>
      <h3>Painted jackets & wearable art</h3>
      <p>Hand-painted military jackets, denim and custom garments built as one-of-one or limited-run wearable pieces.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Browse wearable lane →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lane 03</span>
      <h3>Brand / collaboration direction</h3>
      <p>Campaign visuals, creative direction and culture-first collaborations designed to fit the NO BALL GAMES world without fake name-dropping.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Open collaboration enquiries →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lane 04</span>
      <h3>XRP KIDs / XRPL lore branch</h3>
      <p>Canon lane for XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG. Treat this as internal canon unless issuer and marketplace records are verified.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Read XRP lane →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lane 05</span>
      <h3>NO BALL GAMES archive / research</h3>
      <p>Truth files, source gaps, rights policy and claim discipline that keep public pages credible and proof-led.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>Open archive lane →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Publishing discipline</span>
      <h2>Build the lane, then publish the proof.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Use internal canon labels for lore-heavy project narratives.</li>
        <li>Mark source-needed claims before presenting them as fact.</li>
        <li>Avoid unverified token and marketplace metrics.</li>
        <li>Keep project copy direct, streetwise and culturally grounded.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Next actions</span>
      <h2>Where collaborators can plug in.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Collectors: register interest in originals and wearables.</li>
        <li>Artists: submit work for co-creation lanes.</li>
        <li>Lore contributors: help map canon pages and timeline detail.</li>
        <li>Source checkers: submit proof links for claim upgrades.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}community/`}>Join community lanes →</a>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
